                    <span class="industry-insight-number">
                        01
                    </span>

                </div>

                <h3>
                    Designing PET packaging with recyclability in mind.
                </h3>

                <p class="industry-insight-summary">
                    Packaging design increasingly considers material
                    selection, closure design and end-of-life recovery
                    as connected decisions.
                </p>

                <details class="industry-insight-details">

                    <summary>
                        Read insight
                    </summary>

                    <p>
                        Responsible PET packaging design considers how
                        bottles, preforms, closures and labels interact
                        with collection and recycling systems. Clear
                        material choices and practical component design
                        can help packaging move more effectively through
                        its full lifecycle.
                    </p>

                </details>

            </article>

            <article class="industry-insight-card">

                <div class="industry-insight-top">

                    <span class="industry-insight-category">
                        Closure innovation
                    </span>

                    <span class="industry-insight-number">
                        02
                    </span>

                </div>

                <h3>
                    Tethered closures continue to influence bottle design.
                </h3>

                <p class="industry-insight-summary">
                    Closure systems are becoming an increasingly
                    important part of packaging usability, efficiency
                    and responsible design.
                </p>

                <details class="industry-insight-details">

                    <summary>
                        Read insight
                    </summary>

                    <p>
                        Tethered closure designs keep the cap connected
                        to the container after opening. For packaging
                        manufacturers, this creates new considerations
                        around neck finishes, closure performance,
                        production capability and the overall customer
                        experience.
                    </p>

                </details>

            </article>

            <article class="industry-insight-card">

                <div class="industry-insight-top">

